> Manipulate integers as sequences of bits.

name: Bitwise
slug: bookshelf-bitwise
version: 5.0.0
tags: runtime


$operands = storage: {
  a: int > first operand
  b: int > second operand
}

$shift = storage: {
  n: int > number to shift
  by: int @ 0..31 > number of positions to shift by
}


feature context_int_provider and > Compute the bitwise AND of two numbers.
  authors: Aksiome, theogiraudet
  created: 2018/02/27 1.13
  updated: 2026/09/18 26.3

  input $operands
  output result: int > a AND b, each bit set when it is set in both


feature context_int_provider or > Compute the bitwise OR of two numbers.
  authors: Aksiome, theogiraudet
  created: 2018/02/27 1.13
  updated: 2026/09/18 26.3

  input $operands
  output result: int > a OR b, each bit set when it is set in either


feature context_int_provider xor > Compute the bitwise XOR of two numbers.
  authors: Aksiome, theogiraudet
  created: 2018/02/27 1.13
  updated: 2026/09/18 26.3

  input $operands
  output result: int > a XOR b, each bit set when it is set in exactly one


feature context_int_provider not > Invert every bit of a number.
  authors: Aksiome, theogiraudet
  created: 2018/08/27 1.13
  updated: 2026/09/18 26.3

  input storage: {
    n: int > number to invert
  }
  output result: int > NOT n, which is -n - 1


feature context_int_provider bit_count > Count the bits set to 1 in a number.
  authors: Aksiome
  created: 2024/02/27 1.20.4
  updated: 2026/09/18 26.3

  input storage: {
    n: int > number to count the bits of
  }
  output result: int @ 0..32 > number of bits set to 1, 32 for -1


feature context_int_provider bit_length > Count the bits needed to represent a number.
  authors: Aksiome, theogiraudet
  created: 2020/09/06 1.16
  updated: 2026/09/18 26.3

  input storage: {
    n: int > number to measure
  }
  output result: int @ 0..32 > position of the highest bit set plus one, 0 for 0 and 32 for a negative number


feature context_int_provider shift_left > Shift the bits of a number to the left.
  authors: Aksiome
  created: 2026/09/18 26.3
  updated: 2026/09/18 26.3

  input $shift
  output result: int > n shifted left, the bits pushed out of the integer dropped


feature context_int_provider shift_right > Shift the bits of a number to the right, keeping its sign.
  authors: Aksiome
  created: 2026/09/18 26.3
  updated: 2026/09/18 26.3

  input $shift
  output result: int > n shifted right, the sign bit filling the freed positions
